Companion (bottom-screen barter) — bring companionBarterCategory to parity with the
Lua itemCategory used by the inventory and looting screens.

The barter categoriser only ever emitted six buckets (weapon/armor/apparel/tools/
consumable/misc), so relative to looting it was missing a Books tab entirely and was
mis-filing three item types into Misc that looting files under Tools:

  Books        ESM::Book        -> was "misc", now "book"   (NEW barter tab; scrolls are
                                   Books in ESM, so they land here too, matching looting's
                                   Books = book + scroll)
  Apparatus    ESM::Apparatus   -> was "misc", now "tools"  (looting: Tools)
  Repair       ESM::Repair      -> was "misc", now "tools"  (looting: Tools)
  Light        ESM::Light       -> was "misc", now "tools"  (looting: Tools — torches were
                                   deliberately moved out of Misc there; this matches it)
  Keys         Class::isKey     -> was "misc", now "key"    (NEW tab on both screens)

Keys use the virtual Class::isKey rather than testing the ESM flag directly: the base
Class::isKey returns false, so non-Miscellaneous types answer correctly with no type check,
and MWClass::Miscellaneous::isKey reads the same ESM::Miscellaneous::Key flag the Lua
`isKey` record property exposes — which ESMStore additionally sets at load for anything a
door/container references as its key. So the two screens agree on what a key is. Gold is
Miscellaneous but not a key, so it still falls through to "misc".

Applied AFTER companion-barter-export / -instance-id / -weight rather than folded into the
export patch: the new #includes sit in the same include block that companion-barter-instance-id
quotes as context for its own <unordered_map> hunk, so editing the export patch there would
break that patch's context lines.

diff --git a/apps/openmw/mwgui/tradewindow.cpp b/apps/openmw/mwgui/tradewindow.cpp
--- a/apps/openmw/mwgui/tradewindow.cpp
+++ b/apps/openmw/mwgui/tradewindow.cpp
@@ -11,12 +11,16 @@
 #include <unordered_map>

 #include <components/esm3/loadalch.hpp>
+#include <components/esm3/loadappa.hpp>
 #include <components/esm3/loadarmo.hpp>
+#include <components/esm3/loadbook.hpp>
 #include <components/esm3/loadclot.hpp>
 #include <components/esm3/loadench.hpp>
 #include <components/esm3/loadingr.hpp>
+#include <components/esm3/loadligh.hpp>
 #include <components/esm3/loadlock.hpp>
 #include <components/esm3/loadmgef.hpp>
 #include <components/esm3/loadprob.hpp>
+#include <components/esm3/loadrepa.hpp>
 #include <components/esm3/loadskil.hpp>
 #include <components/esm3/loadweap.hpp>
@@ -106,20 +110,31 @@
-    // Companion: coarse category matching the bottom-screen barter tabs
-    // (All / Weapons / Armor / Apparel / Tools / Consumables / Misc). Deliberately
-    // coarser than the inventory's fine slot categories — the barter screen groups
-    // into these seven buckets only. Books/lights/apparatus/repair/misc all fall to
-    // "misc" (there is no Books tab on the barter screen).
+    // Companion: coarse category matching the bottom-screen barter tabs
+    // (All / Weapons / Armor / Apparel / Tools / Books / Consumables / Keys / Misc).
+    // Still coarser than the inventory's fine SLOT categories, but the BUCKETS now line
+    // up with the Lua itemCategory behind the inventory/looting tabs, so an item files
+    // under the same tab name on every screen. Anything unclassified falls to "misc".
     const char* companionBarterCategory(const MWWorld::Ptr& item)
     {
         const auto type = item.getType();
         if (type == ESM::Weapon::sRecordId)
             return "weapon";
         if (type == ESM::Armor::sRecordId)
             return "armor";
         if (type == ESM::Clothing::sRecordId)
             return "apparel";
-        if (type == ESM::Lockpick::sRecordId || type == ESM::Probe::sRecordId)
+        // Tools = "carried, not worn, has a use" — the same practical grouping the Lua
+        // itemCategory feeds the inventory/looting Tools tab (lockpick/probe/apparatus/
+        // repair/light), NOT a vanilla taxonomy. Vanilla files torches under Misc.
+        if (type == ESM::Lockpick::sRecordId || type == ESM::Probe::sRecordId
+            || type == ESM::Apparatus::sRecordId || type == ESM::Repair::sRecordId
+            || type == ESM::Light::sRecordId)
             return "tools";
         if (type == ESM::Potion::sRecordId || type == ESM::Ingredient::sRecordId)
             return "consumable";
+        if (type == ESM::Book::sRecordId)
+            return "book";
+        // Keys before the misc fallback: Class::isKey is false on the base class, so this is
+        // safe to ask of any item and only Miscellaneous records with the Key flag answer true.
+        if (item.getClass().isKey(item))
+            return "key";
         return "misc";
     }
